From a60fc154cc1ead1d2766fd4e017eecc3c6da5dfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raold <868138+raold@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:49:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep healers on Valithria and log what they do each pull

Raid healers stayed off the dragon even with the raid at full health, and
holy paladins' stock "reach party member to heal" (ACTION_EMERGENCY + 3)
outranked the dragon heal (ACTION_RAID + 2), so they ran after any hurt
member out of range instead of healing her. Reserved raid healers now heal
her while every member within the party-heal search radius is at 80% or
more, the reach move is suppressed for a healer on the dragon, and Beacon
of Light (raid members only) is no longer offered on her.

Every 5 s while her encounter is in progress, Playerbots.log gets a
valithria_watch line (her health, healer duties, dragon casts) and one
valithria_healer line per bot healer: allocation, current duty, the icc
strategy, health, mana, distance, line of sight, dragon casts, the heal
action's last result, the last spell cast and target, and the last action
the bot executed. It runs from her own update, so it also reports bots
that lack the icc strategy.
